      <title>What's Next Following Monte dei Paschi's High-Stakes Move?</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-08-21/what-s-next-following-paschi-s-high-stakes-move-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">65bcfdbd32402a255c43b02c</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:43:09 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Banca Monte dei Paschi is seeking to buy two separate banks for a combined price of €34 billion ($40 billion) in a defensive move designed to ward off a takeover by rival Intesa Sanpaolo.
The Italian lender said it’s launching an all-share bid for Banco BPM valuing it at €25.3 billion and another one for Banca Generali valuing it at €8.7 billion, based on the market close two days ago, according to a statement Friday. Bloomberg's Tommaso Ebhardt reports from Milan. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
